From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: refuse ring and channel changes on a claimed GMAC

"ethtool -G" and "ethtool -L" reach stmmac_reinit_ringparam() and
stmmac_reinit_queues(), which reopen a running interface with
stmmac_release() and stmmac_open() and send no netdev event on the
way. While qca-dwmac-nss has claimed the GMAC for the NSS firmware,
the release napi_disable()s the queues the claim already disabled and
blocks for good with rtnl held: on a Xiaomi CR8806, "ethtool -G eth1
rx 64" took the router off the network until a power cycle.

MTU changes have the same reopen, but qca-dwmac-nss releases the claim
on NETDEV_PRECHANGEMTU first. Ring and channel changes have no event
to hook, so return -EBUSY while the GMAC is claimed.

Reported-by: fanha99 <fanha99@hotmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/kuncy7/openwrt-nss-edma/issues/52
Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -7729,11 +7729,34 @@ static void stmmac_napi_del(struct net_d
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A claimed GMAC runs on the NSS firmware's descriptor rings. Reopening
+ * it here, as a ring or channel change does, bypasses the netdev
+ * notifiers the owner releases the claim on: stmmac_release() would
+ * napi_disable() the queues the claim already disabled, which blocks for
+ * good with rtnl held. MTU changes go through NETDEV_PRECHANGEMTU
+ * instead; these have no event to hook, so refuse them.
+ */
+static int stmmac_reinit_refuse_claimed(struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	struct stmmac_priv *priv = netdev_priv(dev);
+
+	if (!priv->dp_owner)
+		return 0;
+
+	netdev_warn(dev, "the NSS firmware owns the DMA, not reconfiguring it\n");
+	return -EBUSY;
+}
+
 int stmmac_reinit_queues(struct net_device *dev, u32 rx_cnt, u32 tx_cnt)
 {
 	struct stmmac_priv *priv = netdev_priv(dev);
 	int ret = 0, i;
 
+	ret = stmmac_reinit_refuse_claimed(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	if (netif_running(dev))
 		stmmac_release(dev);
 
@@ -7757,7 +7780,11 @@ int stmmac_reinit_queues(struct net_devi
 int stmmac_reinit_ringparam(struct net_device *dev, u32 rx_size, u32 tx_size)
 {
 	struct stmmac_priv *priv = netdev_priv(dev);
-	int ret = 0;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = stmmac_reinit_refuse_claimed(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	if (netif_running(dev))
 		stmmac_release(dev);
